  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Low-Emissions Shunting Locomotives Feasibility Study, through Enterprise - United States Unknown</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant funds a feasibility study (FS) to support the State Railway of Thailand (SRT) in assessing the viability of acquiring a fleet of low or zero-emissions shunting locations and developing related charging infrastructure to replace traditional diesel shunting locomotives in Thailand. SRT seeks to acquire approximately 36 low or zero-emissions locomotives and related charging or fueling infrastructure for use in Bangkok and other stations and railyards throughout the country. The FS will evaluate battery-electric and other low-emissions locomotive technology options and develop the technical specifications for the required battery charging or refueling infrastructure.</narrative>
  </description>
